@@ 1.2 Architecture Diagram
 **Flow for every task:**
 - Human submits task → Mlawuli
 - Mlawuli → Sibali (cost clearance + payload trim)
 - Sibali → Mlawuli (approved payload + token budget)
 - Mlawuli → Worker Agent (optimized payload)
 - Worker Agent → Mlawuli (completed work)
 - Mlawuli → Sibali (final cost indexing)
 - Mlawuli → Human / Dashboard (result)
+
+> **Implementation Note (Windows Reference Deployment)**  
+> In the reference implementation, Mlawuli and worker agents execute as
+> **persistent Windows services** using NSSM. Inter-agent communication occurs
+> via a **file-based JSON task queue** rather than in-memory RPC. This enables
+> background execution, crash recovery, and survivability across reboot.
 
+### 1.4 Execution Model (Windows Service Mode)
+
+The reference implementation runs all agents as **long-lived PowerShell
+processes** registered as Windows services.
+
+Rules:
+- Agents MUST never exit unless explicitly stopped
+- Infinite execution loops are mandatory
+- Crash recovery is handled by the service manager (NSSM)
+- Agents must tolerate restart at any loop boundary
 
@@ §3.2 Mlawuli — CORE DIRECTIVES
